===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰeygʷ-}}
From {{der|en|enm|diggen||to dig}}, alteration of {{der|en|ang|dīcian||to dig a ditch, to mound up earth}} (compare {{cog|ang|dīcere||digger}}) from {{m|ang|dic|dīc, dīċ|dike, ditch}} from {{der|en|gem-pro|*dīkaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*dīkiją||pool, puddle}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰeygʷ-||to stab, dig}}. Additionally, {{cog|enm|diggen}} may derive from an unrecorded suffixed variant, {{m|ang|*dicgian|*dīcgian}}. Akin to {{cog|da|dige||to dig, raise a dike}}, {{cog|sv|dika||to dig ditches}}. Related to {{cog|fr|diguer|t=to dig}}, from {{cog|frm|diguer}}, from {{cog|fro|dikier}}, itself a borrowing of the same Germanic root (from {{cog|dum|dijc}}). More at [[ditch]], [[dike]].

